 50496999, 50497064, 50497286, 50497410, 50497430, 50497464, 50497488, 50497505, 50497531, 50497593, 50497619, 50497622, 50497634, 50497922, 50497943, 50498095, 50498551, 50498641, 50498685], "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:07:28Z", "created_at_i": 1794323248, "num_comments": 75, "objectID": "50441444", "points": 122, "story_id": 50441444, "title": "Generative AI uses more energy on non-English text", "updated_at": "2026-11-14T18:57:27Z", "url": "https://news.umich.edu/generative-ai-uses-more-energy-on-non-english-text/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "jruohonen"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Italy fines Meta €805M over photo privacy"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://www.rapporteur.com/news/italy-fines-meta-880mn-over-photo-privacy-authority/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_jruohonen", "story_50498063", "front_page"], "author": "jruohonen", "children": [50498434, 50498547, 50498712, 50498720, 50498725, 50498735, 50498775, 50498806, 50498834, 50498929, 50498955, 50498974, 50498976, 50498994, 50499012, 50499053, 50499079, 50499292, 50499517], "created_at": "2026-11-14T16:00:14Z", "created_at_i": 1794672014, "num_comments": 55, "objectID": "50498063", "points": 110, "story_id": 50498063, "title": "Italy fines Meta €805M over photo privacy", "updated_at": "2026-11-14T18:58:53Z", "url": "https://www.rapporteur.com/news/italy-fines-meta-880mn-over-photo-privacy-authority/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "snipedbywifi"}, "story_text": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Hey HN readers!<p>I'm snipedbywifi (<a href=\"https://gitlab.com/snipedbywifi\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://gitlab.com/snipedbywifi</a>), and i've been working on terminactory. Please try it out if you'd like to play a cozy factory game while waiting for long agent tasks to finish!<p>The game is a factory game (overused niche, i know xD), but runs in your terminal. Reason i built it? glad you asked: So basically, it started off with me wanting a terminal-native factory game. Me and the modern 5.5 claude models made a base for the game that I liked, and then i went ham adding features / fixing some minor flaws (like adding claude code hooks so you recieve &quot;telegrams&quot; [the agent's responses], so you can review progress directly in-game). (yes, I had heavy AI assistance, disclaimer!!!)<p>Right now, the game has basic factory features you'd expect from a game like this (build stuff, delete stuff, measure how much you're earning, basic selection tools), along with a few more.. &quot;unexpected&quot; features. This includes a fake in-game browser that has a wiki, fake forums, some fun bits of lore, some more lore, a LOT more lore, and a research graph that shows how many items or how much RP (research points) you'd need to unlock something, and some more QOL features.<p>If anyone actually has this issue / want of a terminal-based game that runs alongside your agents so you don't doomscroll, do you have any suggestions, or additional ideas I could add?<p>It's hosted on GitLab, soo, that's one additional thing i'd like to mention<p>Thanks for reading!! snipedbywifi<p>(p.s. first HN post lol)\n(p.s. p.s. there's a lot of hidden lore in the game, so.. lore-divers? you might like it?)"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: A terminal-native idle factory game, written in Rust with ratatui"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://gitlab.com/snipedbywifi/terminactory"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_snipedbywifi", "story_50497132", "show_hn", "front_page"], "author": "snipedbywifi", "children": [50497787, 50498016, 50498153, 50498192, 50498357, 50498890, 50499613], "created_at": "2026-11-14T14:05:54Z", "created_at_i": 1794665154, "num_comments": 16, "objectID": "50497132", "points": 98, "story_id": 50497132, "story_text": "Hey HN readers!<p>I&#x27;m snipedbywifi (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitlab.com&#x2F;snipedbywifi\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitlab.com&#x2F;snipedbywifi</a>), and i&#x27;ve been working on terminactory. Please try it out if you&#x27;d like to play a cozy factory game while waiting for long agent tasks to finish!<p>The game is a factory game (overused niche, i know xD), but runs in your terminal. Reason i built it? glad you asked: So basically, it started off with me wanting a terminal-native factory game. Me and the modern 5.5 claude models made a base for the game that I liked, and then i went ham adding features &#x2F; fixing some minor flaws (like adding claude code hooks so you recieve &quot;telegrams&quot; [the agent&#x27;s responses], so you can review progress directly in-game). (yes, I had heavy AI assistance, disclaimer!!!)<p>Right now, the game has basic factory features you&#x27;d expect from a game like this (build stuff, delete stuff, measure how much you&#x27;re earning, basic selection tools), along with a few more.. &quot;unexpected&quot; features. This includes a fake in-game browser that has a wiki, fake forums, some fun bits of lore, some more lore, a LOT more lore, and a research graph that shows how many items or how much RP (research points) you&#x27;d need to unlock something, and some more QOL features.<p>If anyone actually has this issue &#x2F; want of a terminal-based game that runs alongside your agents so you don&#x27;t doomscroll, do you have any suggestions, or additional ideas I could add?<p>It&#x27;s hosted on GitLab, soo, that&#x27;s one additional thing i&#x27;d like to mention<p>Thanks for reading!! snipedbywifi<p>(p.s. first HN post lol)\n(p.s. p.s. there&#x27;s a lot of hidden lore in the game, so.. lore-divers? you might like it?)", "title": "Show HN: A terminal-native idle factory game, written in Rust with ratatui", "updated_at": "2026-11-14T18:55:24Z", "url": "https://gitlab.com/snipedbywifi/terminactory"}, {"_hig